IDX 846 PAGE 52 LABEL text STRUCT {'level': 'Body', 'level_index': 4, 'parent_id': 845, 'path_text': 'PART II | NOTE 2. SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES | Foreign Currency Translation', 'depth': 4, 'h1_index_norm': 0, 'sibling_index_norm': 0.0, 'is_first_child': True, 'is_last_child': True}
TEXT 'For all significant foreign operations, the functional currency is the local currency. Assets and liabilities of these operations are translated at the period-end exchange rates. Income statement accounts are translated using the average exchange rates prevailing during the period. Translation adjustments are reflected within accumulated other comprehensive loss (AOCI) in stockholders’ equity. Gains and losses from foreign currency transactions are included in net earnings for the period, except for gains and losses on investments in subsidiaries for which settlement is not planned for the foreseeable future and foreign exchange gains and losses on instruments designated as net investment he'

IDX 849 PAGE 52 LABEL section_header STRUCT {'level': 'H3', 'level_index': 3, 'parent_id': 816, 'path_text': 'PART II | NOTE 2. SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES | Stock-based Compensation', 'depth': 3, 'h1_index_norm': 0, 'sibling_index_norm': 0.7333333333333333, 'is_first_child': False, 'is_last_child': False}
