IDX 850 PAGE 52 LABEL text STRUCT {'level': 'Body', 'level_index': 4, 'parent_id': 849, 'path_text': 'PART II | NOTE 2. SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES | Stock-based Compensation', 'depth': 4, 'h1_index_norm': 0, 'sibling_index_norm': 0.0, 'is_first_child': True, 'is_last_child': False}
TEXT 'We generally measure compensation expense for grants of restricted stock units and performance share units using the value of a share of our stock on the date of grant. We estimate the value of stock option grants using a Black-Scholes valuation model. Generally, stock-based compensation is recognized straight line over the vesting period. Our stock-based compensation expense is recorded in selling, general and administrative (SG&A) expenses and cost of sales in our Consolidated Statements of Earnings and allocated to each reportable segment in our segment results.'

